Engine
- vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache-2.0. The image is
  upstream vLLM's wheel for commit a0d7356b98, the fork's vLLM branch over it and
  the vllm-cmp170hx plugin, all from https://github.com/AlexBrandes/vllm, also
  Apache-2.0 (see that repository's NOTICE), on NVIDIA's CUDA 13.0 Ubuntu 24.04
  base image.
- The plugin's EXL3 codec is adapted from turboderp's ExLlamaV3
  (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3), MIT (copy in
  licenses/ExLlamaV3.LICENSE).
- The plugin's layout, startup guard and seam tooling, and its sm_80 GLM-5.3
  code, are derived from vllm-sm80 by Morrowmake
  (https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx), Apache-2.0.

Model
- GLM-5.3-Flash by Z.AI, MIT (copy in licenses/GLM-5.3-Flash.LICENSE). The EXL3
  checkpoint turboderp/GLM-5.3-Flash-exl3 keeps that licence.
- The DFlash2 drafter incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0:
  non-commercial use only, no redistribution.
- This repository ships no weights: download.sh fetches the checkpoint and the
  drafter from their model pages.

Benchmarks
- Speed tables use the sparkDash protocol (MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash, commit
  3e6d4ef, Apache-2.0); its prompts are used as data with attribution.
- GSM8K (OpenAI, MIT) as distributed with vLLM's tests/evals/gsm8k, HumanEval
  (OpenAI, MIT), and GPQA Diamond (Rein et al., CC BY 4.0) with the prompt and
  answer pattern of OpenAI simple-evals (MIT).

